  "body": "## What changed\n\n- The 4-axis wire cut groups the picked open runs by plane. It stitches the runs of each plane with `stitch_open_runs`, the same stitcher that the 2-axis cuts use.\n- When the runs of a plane close into one ring, that ring is the profile of the plane.\n- Runs that do not close are refused by name. Runs that close into two or more rings are refused by name.\n- On the die side, a face with one opening reads that opening as the profile.\n- A face with two or more rings on the punch side is still refused. The text now says that the edge chains of one ring are stitched.\n- The refusal for a curved wall patch now says what to pick: the top and bottom faces, or the edge chains of each outline.\n- The decision is in `docs/decisions/3209-wire-4axis-stitched-profiles.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\n`wire_ruled::read` refused two or more open runs on one plane. `wire_ruled::profile` refused a face with more than one closed ring. Each refusal told the user to pick the other kind, so no pick reached the generator.\n\n## Tests\n\nAll in `crates/app/tests/wire_fans.rs`:\n\n- `stitched_planar_open_runs_generate_and_verify` (replaces `stitched_planar_open_runs_are_refused_by_name`): four top runs and a bottom face generate, and the wire verify has no problems.\n- `stitched_runs_on_both_planes_generate_and_verify`: four runs on each plane generate and verify.\n- `open_runs_that_do_not_close_are_refused_by_name`: three sides of a square give \"3 open runs at Z24.000 ... do not close\".\n- `die_face_reads_its_one_hole_ring_and_verifies`: a round block with a tapered opening generates on the die side. The path stays inside the opening (reach below 8.5 mm, the outer ring is at 20 mm). The wire verify has no problems.\n- `punch_face_with_an_opening_is_refused_by_name`: the same faces on the punch side are refused.\n\nRed before the fix: the first four pins failed with the issue's own refusal texts. The punch pin failed on the old text.\n\nMutations:\n\n- Old `wire_ruled.rs` put back: 5 pins red. Restored: green.\n- Die-only guard relaxed to any side: `punch_face_with_an_opening_is_refused_by_name` red. Restored: green.\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` green (app lib, setup_align_non_mill, wire_4axis, wire_fans, wire_stamp, wire_verify_tol). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The owner's part `sam/sam_edm_part.step` and the EDM-T3 parts are not in the repository. The pins use synthetic meshes of the same kinds: a square outline as four runs, and a tapered opening in a block.\n- The refusal for runs that close into two or more rings has no pin.\n- The guard that refuses one ring plus a stray run on the same plane (`consumed.len() == n`) has no pin.\n- The heavy lanes did not run.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes `wire_ruled.rs` or `wire_fans.rs`.\n\nEffort: max\n\nChangelog: Wire 4-axis cuts accept an outline picked as several edge runs on each plane, and a die face's opening, as the upper and lower profiles.\n\nFixes #3209\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
